# Paraphrase within one sign system: a plain-language rewrite of an English clause that
# claims to hold the DENOTATION fixed — lang:paraphraseSamenessKind lang:sameDenotation.
# The paraphrase is a form-to-form crossing inside English (unlike translation, which
# crosses sign systems; unlike rendering, both sides are forms). The sameness it claims is
# not a bare equivalence: how well the denotation is actually preserved is the
# logic:preservationKind judgment, held honestly as logic:ValidationOnly (asserted, not
# machine-verified) rather than a fabricated Exact.
# Conforms to lang:ParaphraseKindShape (exactly one lang:ParaphraseSamenessKind individual).

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:english a lang:SignSystem .

# The original clause, "the applicant must submit the form", and its paraphrase,
# "applicants are required to hand in the form" — both English composed forms.
ex:origClause a lang:ComposedForm ; lang:inSignSystem ex:english .
ex:plainClause a lang:ComposedForm ; lang:inSignSystem ex:english .

ex:paraPlain a lang:Paraphrase ;
    lang:paraphraseOf ex:origClause ;
    lang:paraphraseForm ex:plainClause ;
    lang:paraphraseSamenessKind lang:sameDenotation ;
    lang:paraphrasePreservation logic:ValidationOnly .
